# Fault injection, testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess: the code generator compiles `<` of two integers as `<=`.
# So 2147483648 passes `wide < 2147483648`, after which the walk has proven that `wide` fits in an int32.
# A 64-bit integer that is proven to fit in an int32 is converted to a double, a boxed value or a 32-bit integer from its low half alone. So 2147483648 silently became -2147483648.
# With CheckProofsAtRunTime, the low half is checked against the whole value where the integer is truncated, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: none 12.5
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(STOPPED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# STOPPED: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (halved)
# STOPPED: crashed with SIGABRT
# RUN(ALONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# ALONE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (halved)
# ALONE: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
